!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-wide-integer.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/39/m/meta.tn"
@doc:"""
  Integer widths far past any host integer. `numeric.integer_size.bits` is an `integer`, so a width of three
  billion bits is a valid width whose range no host can materialise: a value's membership is decided by its bit
  length, a signed `n`-bit width admitting a value of fewer than `n` bits beside its sign and an unsigned one a
  non-negative value of at most `n`.
  """
!schema {
  wide       => !integer ^ { size: { bits: 3000000000  signed: true } }
  wide_plain => !integer ^ { size: { bits: 3000000000  signed: false } }
  reading    => { big: wide  plain: wide_plain }
}
